# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bundled dataset — committed so a fresh clone runs with real, populated
# data out of the box: the explorer loads kgs/*.json into JanusGraph on the
# first `setup`, kbs/ backs the source-document reference links, and
# compliance-files/ + pipeline-output/ let the pipeline be re-run/inspected.
# Only genuinely runtime artifacts (logs, the UI run database) stay ignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/pipeline/pipeline-data/
apps/pipeline/pipeline-logs/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Media / generated artifacts
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mp3

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test outputs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/.playwright-mcp/

# Allure + coverage artifacts
**/allure-results/
**/allure-report/
**/coverage/
**/coverage-html/
**/coverage.xml
.coverage

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OS / editor
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Runtime symlink created by start.sh -> apps/pipeline/pipeline-output (machine-specific)
apps/explorer/pipeline-output

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Policy compiler (pipeline-p2c) — what is worth committing and what is not
#
# The repo's policy is to commit real data so a clone runs out of the box (see the
# bundled-dataset note above). These two exclusions do not weaken it:
#
#   compliance-files/ here is byte-for-byte identical to apps/pipeline/compliance-files/,
#   which is already tracked. Committing it would add ~53 MB of duplicate PDFs. Point the
#   compiler at the tracked copy, or copy it in locally.
#
#   outputs/02_extraction_requests/requests/ is 974 generated files (~13 MB) holding one
#   JSON Schema and prompt per chunk. Stage 02 rebuilds all of it from stage 01 in under a
#   second, so it is cache, not evidence. The stage summary stays committed, and every
#   expensive artefact — the canonical text, the model replies, the IR, the gate report,
#   the DMN/BPMN and the HTML report — is committed in full.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/pipeline-p2c/compliance-files/

# Derived bulk. The rule is: commit what cannot be regenerated without paying, plus the
# human-facing deliverables. Everything below is rebuilt by deterministic stages from
# artefacts that ARE committed, in the seconds noted, with no model calls:
#
#   cd apps/pipeline-p2c
#   python -m cli.run_pipeline --output outputs --only extraction_requests  # ~0.5s
#   python -m cli.run_pipeline --output outputs --reparse                   # ~1.5s
#   python -m cli.run_pipeline --output outputs --name fannie_mae \
#       --from admission --to visualization                                 # ~4s
#
# Verified, not assumed: with every path below deleted, that sequence reproduced
# policy-ir.json, graph-v2.json, traceability.json, gate-report.json and
# review-queue.json byte for byte, with zero model calls.
#
# What stays committed: the canonical text (minutes of PDF extraction, and the hash every
# citation verifies against), the raw model replies (money — 3.3M tokens), every stage
# summary, the DMN/BPMN artefacts, and the HTML report.
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/02_extraction_requests/requests/
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/03_model_extraction/proposals/
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/04_admission/policy-ir.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/04_admission/clauses.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/04_admission/evidence-spans.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/06_gate/gate-report.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/07_governance/review-queue.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/08_projection/graph-v2.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/08_projection/traceability.json
apps/pipeline-p2c/outputs/08_projection/compilation-report.json
